              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōs, mōris — \"a custom, a way; (plural) character, morals\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hic mōs antīquus est. This is an old custom."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōs, mōris m. The plural mōrēs is a person's ways, his character. Mōs maiōrum, the custom of the ancestors. English moral and morals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of mōs is not settled; Lewis & Short give no sure account. English moral comes from its adjective mōrālis."
            }
          ]
        },
